anisms within the diachronic register: (1) *Stimmung*-saturation, modulating the *input* to *doxa* — a sustained higher-order *pathos* persists as a tonal coloring that biases subsequent perception; the angry person sees enemies in shadows because the anger-*Stimmung* re-saturates the perceptual encounter. (2) Corrective-faculty impairment (the mechanism Aristotle specifies in *De Insomniis*), modulating the *gating* of *doxa* — emotional excitement disables the controlling sense, so that *phantasmata* that would normally be intercepted pass into *doxa* unopposed. Both are diachronic modulations of synchronic transitions, not new synchronic transitions. Mechanism (1) modulates basic valence at $A_0$ as a function of prior actualizations; mechanism (2) modulates the *doxa*-gate's content-conditionality.\n\n(E) **The *hexis*/*Geworfenheit* temporality framing** (~700 words) — develops the closing argument that the diachronic register is *pathos*-grade thrownness. Open with the Aristotelian articulation: *hexis* as \"settled disposition,\" formed through repeated actualization. Quote *NE* II.1, 1103a14–b2 (\"moral excellence comes about as a result of habit\"; \"we become builders by building, lyre-players by playing the lyre, just by doing just acts, temperate by doing temperate acts, brave by doing brave acts\"). Argue that each actualization of a *pathos*-chain leaves a residual modification of the dispositional ground; over time, repeated actualizations consolidate into *hexeis* that condition subsequent chain-actualizations. *Hexis* is not a third stage of the chain but the temporal sedimentation of repeated chain-actualizations into a dispositional ground. Develop the Heideggerian articulation: *Being and Time* §29 establishes that state-of-mind has three essential characteristics (it discloses Dasein in its thrownness; it has already disclosed Being-in-the-world as a whole; it discloses worldhood in the mode of circumspective concern), and that thrownness names 